          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Why does she have to weigh herself every day?",
          "answer": "Daily weighing is mainly used to spot **fluid retention**, which is when the body holds extra water. The reason it matters depends on the condition, so I can't tell you her specific reason without knowing what she has. Her care team can explain that.\n\n**Heart failure:** When the heart doesn't pump or fill well, fluid can build up. The heart failure guidance says weight gain over days \"reflects retained fluid rather than tissue.\" Weight often rises before swelling or breathlessness appears, so it gives an early warning. (Sources: *Heart failure*, condition summary; *Diet and fluid in heart failure*, lifestyle guidance.)\n\n**Kidney disease:** My search didn't return any passage on daily weighing for kidney disease, so I can't describe that reason from the material I have.\n\n**How a daily change is read:**\n- Weigh at the same time each day, after using the bathroom and before eating, on the same scale, and write the number down.\n- The heart failure guidance says a gain of a few pounds (about 2 to 3 kilograms) over two or three days is a fluid signal and a reason to contact the care team. It also describes a larger gain over a week as a fluid signal.\n- Her clinician may have set specific numbers for her. Those take priority over general figures.\n\n**Seek urgent help if:**\n- Weight rises quickly over a few days, especially with worse breathlessness or swelling.\n- She is breathless at rest, or wakes up breathless and it doesn't settle when she sits up.\n- She has chest pain, fainting, a very fast or irregular pulse with symptoms, or sudden confusion.\n- She coughs up pink frothy spit with severe breathlessness. This is an emergency.\n\nIn those cases, call your local emergency number.\n\n**To clarify:** Which condition does she have? If it is heart failure, the points above apply. If it is kidney disease or something else, tell me and I'll search for guidance on that condition.\n\n*Educational information only. This does not diagnose or treat, and it should not guide real medical decisions.*\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
