          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What about salt?",
          "answer": "Here is a brief overview of salt (sodium) while you decide what you'd like to know.\n\n[removed: this system does not give doses or amounts.] Any reduction helps, even if the target isn't reached. *(Source: Diet for high blood pressure.)*\n\n**Where sodium comes from:** Most dietary sodium is not from the salt shaker. The large majority is in packaged and restaurant foods, including:\n- Bread\n- Processed meat\n- Cheese\n- Sauces\n- Soups\n- Snacks\n- Prepared meals\n\nCooking from unprocessed ingredients and checking the sodium per serving on food labels are described as more effective than any single swap. *(Source: Diet for high blood pressure.)*\n\n**If your mother has heart failure:** Sodium limits there are set individually. The guidance says very strict limits can worsen appetite and nutrition in people who are already eating poorly, so her clinician should set her target. *(Source: Diet and fluid in heart failure.)*\n\n**What would you like to know?** For example:\n- How much sodium is in particular foods or meals\n- How sodium relates to blood pressure\n- Sodium limits for heart failure or another condition\n- Practical tips for cutting back\n\n*Educational information only. This does not diagnose or treat, and it should not guide real medical decisions.*\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
